$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 4-Allylisoindoline•HCl. A 3 L flask equipped with overhead stirring, an
addition funnel and a thermocouple was purged with N2, then charged under
positive N2 pressure with 2•HCl (100 g, 0.426 mol), Pd(OAc)2 (0.48 g,
2.13 mmol) and (neopentyl)tBu2P•HBF4 (1.3 g, 4.3 mmol). The flask was
then charged with toluene (1.8 L, which had been previously de-oxygenated
via N2 subsurface sparging). Allylmagnesium chloride (800 mL, 1.36
mol,1.7 M in THF) was charged to the addition funnel and then added to
the slurry, with external cooling, over 1 h such that Ti ≤ 25 °C . The
resulting solution was then heated to and maintained at Ti = 45-50 °C for
16 h. After cooling to ambient temperature, the reaction was
inverse-quenched by slow transfer, with external cooling and at a rate
such that Ti is less than 35 °C , into a 3 L jacketed flask (equipped
with a drop valve and overhead stirring) that had been charged with a
solution of 15 wt% citric acid (1.1 L). The organic phase, which
contained 1.2 g of 1 by assay, was rejected. The aqueous phase was
assayed for 61.3 g of 1 (90% yield in organic phase, corresponding to a
92% end of reaction assay yield, along with 2.6% AY of 3). The aqueous
phase was transferred to an extractor, to which was charged fresh toluene
(650 mL) and the resulting biphasic mixture was stirred. Ammonium
hydroxide (28-30% in water, 650 mL) was added at a rate such that Ti ≤ 30
°C , resulting in a pH 10 aqueous phase. 1, yield 92%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM other product(s) also detected, Kumada coupling, optimization study,
optimized on catalyst (ligand, metal/ligand ratio), temperature, solvent
ratio, assay yield determined after stage 2
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Preparation of 4-Allylisoindoline via a Kumada Coupling with
Allylmagnesium Chloride
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Zacuto, Michael J.; Shultz, C. Scott; Journet, Michel
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Process Research & Development (2011), 15(1), 158-161

